# Compose configuration for a local run. Copy to `.env` beside compose.yaml and edit.
#
# This file configures the containers, not the API. The API's own settings still live in
# src/Pictura.Vita.Api/.env.example, and are what a `dotnet run` reads; Compose passes the
# few that differ under Docker as environment variables, which win over that file.

# The host directory holding your timelines. Each timeline is one folder in here, named for
# its id, holding data.v1.json alongside its images/ and narratives/.
#
# It is mounted read-write at /timelines in the API container. Defaults to ./data in this
# repo, which is gitignored.
#
# Your real timelines are identity-grade data and belong outside the working copy — point
# this at wherever you actually keep them.
# PICTURA_VITA_TIMELINES_DIR=/path/to/timelines
